A constraint language $\mathcal{D}$ over a domain $D$ $pp$-constructs a constraint language $\mathcal{E}$ over a domain $E$ if there is a sequence of constraint languages $\mathcal{D} = \mathcal{C}_1,...,\mathcal{C}_k=\mathcal{E}$ such that for each $1\leq i\leq k$
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathcal{C}_i$ $pp$-interprets $\mathcal{C}_{i+1}$, or
