    If $t$ is a constant and $M, N, M', N'$ are parameters chosen so that $M' = \poly(M)$, $M \geq tN + 1$, $M' \geq (t-1)N' + 1$,
    then $\ourPigeon{(t+1)}{M}{N}$ does not have an efficient black-box reduction to $\ourPigeon{t}{M'}{N'}$.
