  \item \label{item:sandwichbasic2} $\mathcal{J}$ is correct as a reduction from $\CSP(\struct{A})$ to  $\PCSP(\struct{S}_1,\struct{S}_2)$ when limited to instances $\struct{X}$ with the property that $\struct{X}$ homomorphically maps to $\struct{A}$ if and only if it homomorphically maps to a substructure of $\struct{A}$ of domain size $\leq n$.  
