\label{fact:approx}
   For nonnegative scalars $a, b, c$, and $d$, the following holds.
   \begin{itemize}
       \item If $a \approx_{\epsilon_1} b$ and $b \approx_{\epsilon_2} c$, then $a \approx_{\epsilon_1 + \epsilon_2} c$.
       \item If $a \approx_{\epsilon} c$ and $b \approx_{\epsilon} d$, then $a + b \approx_{\epsilon} c + d$.
       \item For $0 < \epsilon < 1/2$, if $(1-\epsilon) a \le b \le (1+\epsilon) a$, then $a \approx_{1.5\epsilon} b$.
