\label{def:canonical-uniform}
 Given an instance $J = (V, \cC)$, sample an assignment $b \in D^V$ as follows:
 \begin{itemize}
   \item For each isolated variable $v \in V \setminus V(\cC)$: $\quad b_v \in D^{\set v}$ is independently
     drawn from the uniform distribution over $D$
   \item For each constraint $C \in \cC$: $\quad b_C \in D^{V(C)}$ is independently drawn from $\mu_C$, conditioned
     on agreeing at the common variables shared by multiple constraints
 \end{itemize}
 Then $b \coloneqq \bigcup_{v \in V \setminus V(\cC)} b_v \cup \bigcup_{C \in \cC} b_C$.
 Let $\mu_J$ be the distribution of $b$.

