    Similarly, $G_{v,3}$ have positive prices and therefore can only be sold to agents in $A_v$ and $A_{e,1}$ where $e=(v,k)$ for some $k$ (there can only be a constant number of such edges since the out-degree of each vertex is bounded). Thus by market clearance, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        p(G_{v,3})\leq \frac{(5m^{10} + \Theta(48m^3))(1+\epsilon)}{2m^{10}} = 5/2 + O(1/m^7).
    \end{equation*}
\end{proof}

