  \label{lem:learn_lb}    
  Let $s, t : \N \rightarrow \N$ be size functions such that $n\le s(n)\le t(n)$ and $\eps, \delta$ be parameters such that $\eps<1/2$, $0 \leq \delta \leq 1/9$. 
If for infinitely many input lengths $N=2^n$, $\MCSP[(s,0),(t,\eps)] \notin\Circuit[N \cdot \poly(t(n)/\eps)]$, then for infinitely many inputs $n$, $\Circuit[s(n)]$ cannot be learnt up to error $\eps/2$ with confidence $1-\delta$ by $t(n)$-size circuits using non-adaptive membership queries over the uniform distribution.

