PromiseBQP is the set of promise problems $(\Pi_{\rm YES}, \Pi_{\rm NO})$ that can be solved by a uniform family of quantum circuits. More precisely, it is required that there is a uniform family of quantum circuits $Y_r$ acting on ${\rm poly}(r)$ qubits that decide if a string $x$ of length $r$ is a {\rm YES}-instance or a {\rm NO}-instance in the following sense. The application of $Y_r$ to the computational basis state $\ket{x,0}$ produces the state
\be
\label{result of Yr}
