\label{fprpolydef}
$\mathsf{FP/rpoly}$ is the class of polynomially-bounded relations $R\subseteq \bin^* \times \bin^*$ for which there exists a polynomial-time deterministic classical algorithm $A$, a polynomial $p(n,m)$, and an infinite list of advice distributions $\{\mathcal{D}_{n,m}\}_{n,m\ge 1}$, where $\mathcal{D}_{n,m}$ is supported on $\bin^{p(n,m)}$, such that for all $x$ for which there exists a $y$ such that $(x,y)\in R$ and all $m$,
$$ \Pr_{r \sim \mathcal{D}_{n,m}}[(x,A(x,0^m,r))\in R]\ge 1-\frac{1}{m}.$$

